{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "When building a rails application, sometimes it is quicker to build one code base that is shared on two completely different frontend applications.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/39e79e71b6c17a43c5d0e34250e72eda10fd73dd9c14b9072014402d85b1f958.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.62], [3, 0.62, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 1.42], [5, 1.94, 2.28], [6, 2.28, 2.5], [7, 2.5, 2.62], [8, 2.62, 2.86], [9, 2.86, 3.08], [10, 3.08, 3.36], [11, 3.36, 3.64], [12, 3.64, 3.94], [13, 3.94, 4.2], [14, 4.2, 4.42], [15, 4.42, 4.54], [16, 4.54, 4.84], [17, 4.84, 5.06], [18, 5.06, 5.32], [19, 5.32, 5.76], [20, 5.76, 6.22], [22, 6.7, 7.04]]}, {"text": "I am going to discuss the design approaches I used to segregate the two rails websites within a single rails application base.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/16c2ca3d60c89d8856e4e35abda6b9d02b08140841327ec9dc9cd3184d46a3be.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.16], [6, 1.16, 1.42], [7, 1.42, 1.82], [8, 1.82, 2.06], [10, 2.3, 2.5], [11, 2.5, 3.06], [12, 3.06, 3.18], [13, 3.18, 3.36], [14, 3.36, 3.58], [15, 3.58, 4.04], [17, 4.46, 4.54], [18, 4.54, 4.8], [19, 4.8, 5.2], [20, 5.2, 5.64], [21, 5.64, 5.96]]}, {"text": "Configuring the Front End", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ef67a0f50da5ba92a083a1a2139ac43dc8e12c0b55b3a986479f8459ce5b7811.mp3"}, {"text": "My first ‘trick’ is to build the system such that all interactions are run through an RESTful API.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c8e701b3d336845657f38a33757f6ff78701c762cf3c1184eeda696d43794416.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.76], [2, 0.76, 1.18], [3, 1.18, 1.58], [4, 1.58, 1.72], [5, 1.72, 1.94], [6, 1.94, 2.1], [8, 2.5, 2.86], [9, 2.86, 3.04], [10, 3.04, 3.26], [11, 3.26, 3.84], [12, 3.84, 4.1], [13, 4.1, 4.3], [14, 4.3, 4.56], [16, 4.66, 5.1], [17, 5.1, 5.48]]}, {"text": "This gives one surface area for applications (front end apps or mobile or whatever) and it reduces the amount of duplication that maybe experienced across the two different websites.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/38cca374dcfc1d1116cedffb0065ebae0849a7ffcd22295e7177099de25a44f6.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.28], [5, 1.28, 1.46], [6, 1.46, 2.02], [7, 2.62, 2.86], [9, 3.14, 3.44], [10, 3.44, 3.6], [11, 3.6, 3.82], [12, 3.82, 4.04], [13, 4.04, 4.4], [14, 4.6, 4.9], [15, 4.9, 5.0], [16, 5.0, 5.34], [17, 5.34, 5.56], [18, 5.56, 5.76], [19, 5.76, 5.92], [20, 5.92, 6.46], [21, 6.46, 6.62], [23, 6.86, 7.32], [24, 7.32, 7.64], [25, 7.64, 7.88], [26, 7.88, 8.08], [27, 8.08, 8.34], [28, 8.34, 8.78]]}, {"text": "For my projects, I lean towards AngularJS, mainly because there is a strong community backing the technology, not to mention this is one of Google’s babies.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/804cd1131613a6f2b92b671c8cfb5834b594f39c9af6ec4f18a2ea4c5064aed4.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.14], [1, 0.14, 0.26], [2, 0.26, 0.7], [3, 1.04, 1.12], [4, 1.12, 1.26], [5, 1.26, 1.58], [6, 1.58, 2.58], [7, 3.06, 3.24], [8, 3.24, 3.64], [9, 3.64, 3.88], [10, 3.88, 4.02], [11, 4.02, 4.08], [12, 4.08, 4.36], [13, 4.36, 5.0], [14, 5.0, 5.58], [15, 5.58, 5.78], [16, 5.78, 6.38], [17, 6.84, 7.1], [18, 7.1, 7.24], [19, 7.24, 7.52], [20, 7.52, 7.76], [21, 7.76, 7.9], [22, 7.9, 8.06], [23, 8.06, 8.16], [24, 8.16, 8.58], [25, 8.58, 8.84]]}, {"text": "Both of these websites will have a unique look and feel as well as style sheets and html designs.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/44fae6153d62c100fca80003b832ee8d130a78a34c43feb4880cd0a6a6294f11.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.34], [6, 1.34, 1.48], [7, 1.48, 1.72], [8, 1.72, 2.02], [9, 2.02, 2.26], [10, 2.26, 2.52], [11, 2.52, 2.8], [12, 2.8, 2.96], [13, 2.96, 3.14], [14, 3.14, 3.44], [15, 3.44, 3.76], [16, 3.76, 4.06], [17, 4.06, 4.48], [18, 4.48, 5.02]]}, {"text": "Break apart the CSS files", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/de2645b29747acb69684a26f37eaef546916efab2164c101f291a0e153a06b64.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.76], [3, 0.76, 1.08], [4, 1.08, 1.56]]}, {"text": "I divided my assets/stylesheets folder to look like this:", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/36f05dfd2bd854b215624f54bcff880d8d846d57d0affd9f532d69e06792734e.mp3"}, {"text": "```css application.css /* *= require_self */", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/64d6b53b1a2494621fba599849c84c1cd89dcce168ad131d35562facb5405785.mp3"}, {"text": "Here I am explicitly including the app1.css resources in app1.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5fd1d3c74b2a27f69a8469ff20505d37b9891288012b3bed3af8cd6ba154e787.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.46], [3, 0.46, 0.86], [4, 0.86, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 1.66], [7, 2.8, 3.24], [8, 3.24, 3.64], [9, 3.64, 4.06]]}, {"text": "application.css will include styling that is shared between the two applications.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f3183e99422b3a1bfd7c10cc77a8400fcbf0a562ac9c151cfe84c6b7ad9391da.mp3", "words": [[1, 1.3, 1.58], [2, 1.58, 1.86], [3, 1.86, 2.38], [4, 2.38, 2.62], [5, 2.62, 2.74], [6, 2.74, 2.96], [7, 2.96, 3.28], [8, 3.28, 3.46], [9, 3.46, 3.6], [10, 3.6, 4.16]]}, {"text": "An example, might be your frameworks like bootstrap.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9754b88a779381737de6fb7734c4b17aa26dfda8ddb2bed1bccefc92ea78adcf.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.12], [5, 1.12, 1.48], [6, 1.48, 1.82], [7, 1.82, 2.46]]}, {"text": "appN.css will include the styles that are unique to your web application.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9ea45c43d48b4786aaffc6a659e8198318c7291d8f18164b163df8aadc1a7907.mp3", "words": [[1, 1.16, 1.6], [2, 1.6, 1.9], [3, 1.9, 2.1], [4, 2.1, 2.44], [5, 2.44, 2.6], [6, 2.6, 2.7], [7, 2.7, 2.96], [8, 2.96, 3.2], [9, 3.2, 3.32], [10, 3.32, 3.46], [11, 3.46, 4.02]]}, {"text": "You should create an /assets/stylesheets/app1/ folder to house all of your style sheets for that specific app.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fe35b3b7efeda8419d13f2eb21e576e7f58855393cc7f395ebe67a2e5549818d.mp3"}, {"text": "In my layouts view, you will only want to be loading app1 and application when a user requests an app1 website and app2 and application when the user requests an app2 website.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fa9604940439c335d04558d01b085e89447d01b381bb389cf5ddfa8f1330c094.mp3"}, {"text": "By checking the request host, you can determine the domain the user is on you can decide which css files need to be delivered to the client.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f5bb3b12acfebc344efe574ef22ab49ab7bf6f351ecdab872f52184e6fce6655.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.68], [3, 0.68, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.42], [5, 1.86, 1.92], [6, 1.92, 2.06], [7, 2.06, 2.48], [8, 2.48, 2.72], [9, 2.72, 3.02], [10, 3.02, 3.28], [11, 3.28, 3.6], [12, 3.6, 3.84], [13, 3.84, 4.06], [14, 4.52, 4.7], [15, 4.7, 4.82], [16, 4.82, 5.12], [17, 5.12, 5.42], [18, 5.42, 5.88], [19, 5.88, 6.44], [20, 6.44, 6.7], [21, 6.7, 6.88], [22, 6.88, 6.98], [23, 6.98, 7.28], [24, 7.28, 7.48], [25, 7.48, 7.58], [26, 7.58, 7.88]]}, {"text": "The host check should be offloaded to a helper method that would like:", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9234f5143e542d4f0249c87800abf2b928037bb12829736d5361f6091b009ce7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.14], [1, 0.14, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 1.66], [7, 1.66, 1.82], [8, 1.82, 2.04], [9, 2.04, 2.4], [10, 2.4, 2.62], [11, 2.62, 2.72], [12, 2.72, 2.94]]}, {"text": "In the rails views layout folder, you only include the style sheets that are used", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/83936705a572b61dcc7f31949efa4d920b2d867bb35f2d9a25921f8518cd9677.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.28], [2, 0.28, 0.52], [3, 0.52, 0.94], [5, 1.12, 1.52], [6, 1.98, 2.06], [7, 2.06, 2.32], [8, 2.32, 2.68], [9, 2.68, 2.82], [10, 2.82, 3.16], [11, 3.16, 3.38], [12, 3.38, 3.66], [13, 3.66, 3.76], [14, 3.76, 4.16]]}, {"text": "```ruby layout.html.slim == stylesheet_link_tag “application”, :media => ‘all’", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f5f77493fc23a96b81b2f23b955c3d4d25a8de76c981e3639b13bd59054542b8.mp3"}, {"text": "if app1?", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8f1e30f08558b063c021f24e0a08304e890ef4bc2dd3c2c5fc8320244139f2b8.mp3"}, {"text": "== stylesheet_link_tag “app1”, :media => ‘all’", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ddc8e065bd1ac5fce2ffc2e37be2aba8841aaa54e669f5b6d2e9ee37921e0e8d.mp3"}, {"text": "elsif app2?", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b6a70fbb72a4281f9d18218e2bc9c94d723d1cc214c7e9388df881402a48035f.mp3"}, {"text": "== stylesheet_link_tag “app2”, :media => ‘all’ ```", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f2c742b1c3e35fa3ba504ef3efa30a815247149b6bd1bd281a6a081abf19812e.mp3"}, {"text": "You need to tell rails to precompile these new css files", "block": 17, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9a7bbdeea6d388d39e5ce647c8b17223ecb7b572fdbed5f69d8eae11eac61f91.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.62], [4, 0.62, 0.86], [5, 0.86, 1.14], [7, 1.7, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.16], [9, 2.16, 2.6], [10, 2.6, 3.16]]}, {"text": "```ruby config/initializers/assets.rb Rails.application.config.assets.precompile += %w( app1.css app2.css )", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/399a19bb4a4a6774f187847c761cbafd34fc41c37071bd1027595a6e993be766.mp3"}, {"text": "Don’t forget to tell rails to precompile these new assets.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9f2c28f28f70fdbf9c3c4008266ff449636b660a631753d3adcbd293e02e47a1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.72], [4, 0.72, 0.96], [5, 0.96, 1.22], [7, 1.74, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.12], [9, 2.12, 2.46]]}, {"text": "ruby config/initializers/assets.rb Rails.application.config.assets.precompile += %w( app1.js app2.js )", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a0ac1307711164ae895b9aef47c2b0f444b030230feccef1fe4bb402e4e65a63.mp3"}, {"text": "Backend", "block": 21, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/466faa2bc01ef54dfcd3369c9fa1bae0eb5f5b6242abbfa271c44ba4e811f255.mp3"}, {"text": "If you want to turn certain features on and off for certain applications, you should use the rollout gem.", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/03175a48a475b5cd3cdf6309cedc502955609c65360753f9e2ebd789da622456.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.26], [2, 0.26, 0.42], [3, 0.42, 0.58], [4, 0.58, 0.74], [5, 0.74, 1.06], [6, 1.06, 1.44], [7, 1.44, 1.74], [8, 1.74, 1.86], [9, 1.86, 2.04], [10, 2.04, 2.28], [11, 2.28, 2.54], [12, 2.54, 3.14], [13, 3.66, 3.74], [14, 3.74, 3.92], [15, 3.92, 4.14], [16, 4.14, 4.3], [17, 4.3, 4.68], [18, 4.68, 4.92]]}, {"text": "It is a great tool for enabling and disabling features on the fly, or just completely locking up certain parts of the application.", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fc8e947623e931fbc88acecb9b6cbc890d88b29c07c994d8be2b1683a1737a4e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.42], [3, 0.42, 0.62], [4, 0.62, 0.92], [5, 0.92, 1.1], [6, 1.1, 1.58], [7, 1.58, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.5], [9, 2.5, 2.98], [10, 2.98, 3.28], [11, 3.28, 3.42], [12, 3.42, 3.7], [13, 4.16, 4.24], [14, 4.24, 4.42], [15, 4.42, 4.98], [16, 4.98, 5.36], [17, 5.36, 5.58], [18, 5.58, 5.9], [19, 5.9, 6.2], [20, 6.2, 6.36], [21, 6.36, 6.5], [22, 6.5, 7.0]]}]}